  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Emergency Relief for IDPs and Vulnerable Communities in Yambio Diocese</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Following the event that happened in December 28th along Yambio Maridi road that involved military confrontations between the armed youth and Sudan People&apos;s Liberation Army (SPLA) soldiers that brought untold suffering and misery among the people of Yambio County, many people lost their lives, property with majority being displaced into the nearby bushes and  Yambio town.
Yambio Primary School locally known as Nabima Primary School is hosting thousands of these IDPs. Registration and verification of IDPs is on-going in this school by most of the humanitarian agencies based in Yambio. CDTY would like to support the most vulnerable households with food items. A total of 1,000 households are being targeted for this emergency assistance since the population is so huge and other partners are also playing their part. 
CDTY acknowledges the receipt of &#xa3;50,00 from Caritas Germany and $3,000 from Caritas Belgium for the emergency support to the IDPs.</narrative>
  </description>
